    "description": "Shark Tooth Fossil Lot - 3 Pieces\nWhat A Earth, Natural History & Paleontology Specimens\nFossilized Shark Teeth, Eocene to Cretaceous Era\nThis collection features three authentic fossilized shark tooth specimens, individually mounted in clear hinged display cases over blue foam inserts. Each specimen exhibits distinct anatomical features including intact roots, cusps, and enamel characteristic of prehistoric lamniform shark species. Packaged by What A Earth with educational background information on the reverse, these specimens offer great appeal for fossil enthusiasts, geology classrooms, and specimen collectors.\nItems Included:\nFossil Shark Tooth 1 - Central triangular tooth with wide root and defined enamel crown, housed in clear plastic case\nFossil Shark Tooth 2 - Symmetrical crown with intact root lobes and light brown mineralization, housed in clear plastic case\nFossil Shark Tooth 3 - Pointed crown with lateral cusplets and root structure, housed in clear plastic case\nCondition:\nTeeth are in good fossilized condition with natural mineral preservation, sharp tip edges, and stable root matrix. Clear plastic display cases show light surface scuffs from handling and retail price stickers on the back cards with no cracks to the acrylic housings.",
